{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Part of this video is sponsored by LastPass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2140,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More about last pass at the end of the show."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4560,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The butter fly effect is the idea that the tiny causes, like a flay of a butter fly's wings in Brazil,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10280,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can have huge effects, like setting off a tornado in Texas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that idea comes straight from the title of a scientific paper published nearly 50 years ago"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20040,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and perhaps more than any other recent scientific concept, it has captured the public imagination"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25560,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean on IMDB there is not one but 61"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "different movies, TV episodes, and short films with 'butterfly effect' in the title"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33480,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not to mention prominent references in movies like Jurassic Park, or in songs, books, and memes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39400,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh the memes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41080,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in pop culture the butterfly effect has come to mean"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43800,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that even tiny, seemingly insignificant choices you make can have huge consequences later on in your life"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50240,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I think the reason people are so fascinated by the butterfly effect is because it gets at a fundamental question"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56560,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is, how well can we predict the future?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60040,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the goal of this video is to answer that question by examining the science behind the butterfly effect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66080,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if you go back to the late 1600s, after Isaac Newton had come up with his laws of motion and universal gravitation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73080,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everything seemed predictable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75080,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean we could explain the motions of all the planets and moons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78480,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we could predict eclipses and the appearances of comets with pinpoint accuracy centuries in advance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83960,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "French physicist Pierre-Simon Laplace summed it up in a famous thought experiment:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88240,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he imagined a super-intelligent being, now called Laplace's demon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92400,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that knew everything about the current state of the universe:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95560,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the positions and momenta of all the particles and how they interact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if this intellect were vast enough to submit the data to analysis, he concluded,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the future, just like the past, would be present before its eyes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110680,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is total determinism: the view that the future is already fixed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115520,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We just have to wait for it to manifest itself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118520,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think if you've studied a bit of physics, this is the natural viewpoint to come away with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122680,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean sure there's Heisenberg's uncertainty principle from quantum mechanics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126200,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that's on the scale of atoms;"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128800,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Pretty insignificant on the scale of people."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131760,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Virtually all the problems I studied were ones that could be solved analytically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135920,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like the motion of planets, or falling objects, or pendulums"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139840,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and speaking of pendulums I want to look at a case of a simple pendulum here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144960,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to introduce an important representation of dynamical systems, which is phase space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150080,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so some people may be familiar with position-time or velocity-time graphs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154000,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but what if we wanted to make a 2d plot that represents every possible state of the pendulum?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158880,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every possible thing it could do in one graph"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161800,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well on the x-axis we can plot the angle of the pendulum,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164920,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and on the y-axis its velocity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167080,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is what's called phase space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169320,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the pendulum has friction it will eventually slow down and stop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173000,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this is shown in phase space by the inward spiral --"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176280,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the pendulum swings slower and less far each time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180160,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it doesn't really matter what the initial conditions are,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183040,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we know that the final state will be the pendulum at rest hanging straight down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187400,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and from the graph it looks like the system is attracted to the origin, that one fixed point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192640,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so this is called a fixed point attractor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195120,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now if the pendulum doesn't lose energy, well it swings back and forth the same way each time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200040,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in phase space we get a loop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202200,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the pendulum is going fastest at the bottom but the swing is in opposite directions as it goes back and forth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208200,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the closed loop tells us the motion is periodic and predictable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212240,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anytime you see an image like this in phase space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215440,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know that this system regularly repeats"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218160,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can swing the pendulum with different amplitudes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220600,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the picture in phase space is very similar, just a different sized loop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224880,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now an important thing to note is that the curves never cross in phase space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229240,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's because each point uniquely identifies the complete state of the system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233600,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that state has only one future"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236120,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so once you've defined the initial state, the entire future is determined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240920,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now the pendulum can be well understood using Newtonian physics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but Newton himself was aware of problems that did not submit to his equations so easily,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249240,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "particularly the three-body problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251480,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so calculating the motion of the Earth around the Sun was simple enough with just those two bodies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256160,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but add in one more, say the moon,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258640,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it became virtually impossible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260960,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Newton told his friend Haley that the theory of the motions of the moon made his head ache,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265720,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and kept him awake so often that he would think of it no more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269440,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the problem, as would become clear to Henri Poincaré two hundred years later,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273600,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was that there was no simple solution to the three-body problem"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277080,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Poincaré had glimpsed what later became known as chaos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286400,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chaos really came into focus in the 1960s,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289280,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when meteorologist Ed Lorenz tried to make a basic computer simulation of the Earth's atmosphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294040,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he had 12 equations and 12 variables, things like temperature, pressure, humidity and so on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299680,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the computer would print out each time step as a row of 12 numbers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303560,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you could watch how they evolved over time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now the breakthrough came when Lorenz wanted to redo a run"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as a shortcut he entered the numbers from halfway through a previous printout"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314400,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then he set the computer calculating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 316560,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he went off to get some coffee, and when he came back and saw the results,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320040,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lorenz was stunned."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321840,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The new run followed the old one for a short while but then it diverged"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326160,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and pretty soon it was describing a totally different state of the atmosphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329720,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean totally different weather"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331840,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lorenz's first thought, of course, was that the computer had broken"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334840,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe a vacuum tube had blown."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336600,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But none had."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338120,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The real reason for the difference came down to the fact that printer rounded to three decimal places"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342600,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whereas the computer calculated with six"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345080,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when he entered those initial conditions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347760,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the difference of less than one part in a thousand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350520,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "created totally different weather just a short time into the future"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353920,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now Lorenz tried simplifying his equations and then simplifying them some more,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357760,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down to just three equations and three variables"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360800,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which represented a toy model of convection:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363400,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "essentially a 2d slice of the atmosphere heated at the bottom and cooled at the top"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367840,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but again, he got the same type of behavior:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370720,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if he changed the numbers just a tiny bit, results diverged dramatically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375520,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lorenz's system displayed what's become known as sensitive dependence on initial conditions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380560,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is the hallmark of chaos"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382680,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now since Lorenz was working with three variables, we can plot the phase space of his system in three dimensions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389640,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can pick any point as our initial state and watch how it evolves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Does our point move toward a fixed attractor?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397280,
    "dDurationMs": 1160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or a repeating loop?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 399160,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It doesn't seem to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400680,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In truth, our system will never revisit the same exact state again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406200,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here I actually started with three closely spaced initial states,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410440,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they've been evolving together so far, but now they're starting to diverge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415960,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From being arbitrarily close together, they end up on totally different trajectories."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420840,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is sensitive dependence on initial conditions in action."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424720,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now I should point out that there is nothing random at all about this system of equations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429680,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's completely deterministic, just like the pendulum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432800,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if you could input exactly the same initial conditions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436920,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you would get exactly the same result"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439520,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the problem is, unlike the pendulum, this system is chaotic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443520,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so any difference in initial conditions, no matter how tiny,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447280,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "will be amplified to a totally different final state"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451360,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It seems like a paradox, but this system is both deterministic and unpredictable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because in practice, you could never know the initial conditions with perfect accuracy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462520,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I'm talking infinite decimal places."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465720,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the result suggests why even today with huge supercomputers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469080,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's so hard to forecast the weather more than a week in advance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472840,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, studies have shown that by the eighth day of a long-range forecast,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477040,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the prediction is less accurate than if you just took the historical average conditions for that day"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483280,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and knowing about chaos, meteorologists no longer make just a single forecast"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488360,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead they make ensemble forecasts,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491240,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "varying initial conditions and model parameters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 493880,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to create a set of predictions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496680,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now far from being the exception to the rule, chaotic systems have been turning up everywhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501560,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The double pendulum, just two simple pendulums connected together, is chaotic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506600,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "here two double pendulums have been released simultaneously"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509800,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with almost the same initial conditions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 512760,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but no matter how hard you try,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515160,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you could never release a double pendulum and make it behave the same way twice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519680,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its motion will forever be unpredictable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523920,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you might think that chaos always requires a lot of energy or irregular motions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528800,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this system of five fidgets spinners with repelling magnets in each of their arms is chaotic too"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535920,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At first glance the system seems to repeat regularly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539000,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but if you watch more closely, you'll notice some strange motions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543320,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a spinner suddenly flips the other way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 546120,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even our solar system is not predictable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548640,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a study simulating our solar system for a hundred million years into the future"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553080,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "found its behavior as a whole to be chaotic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556200,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a characteristic time of about four million years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559760,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that means within say 10 or 15 million years,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563400,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some planets or moons may have collided or been flung out of the solar system entirely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569000,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The very system we think of as the model of order,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572600,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is unpredictable on even modest timescales"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576080,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how well can we predict the future?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578560,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not very well at all at least when it comes to chaotic systems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581600,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The further into the future you try to predict the harder it becomes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586080,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and past a certain point, predictions are no better than guesses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590280,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The same is true when looking into the past of chaotic systems and trying to identify initial causes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596240,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think of it kind of like a fog that sets in the further we try to look into the future or into the past"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602800,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chaos puts fundamental limits on what we can know about the future of systems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606880,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what we can say about their past"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609360,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is a silver lining"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611480,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's look again at the phase space of Lorenz's equations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615320,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we start with a whole bunch of different initial conditions and watch them evolve,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619640,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "initially the motion is messy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621800,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But soon all the points have moved towards or onto an object"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625680,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the object, coincidentally, looks a bit like a butterfly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629120,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is the attractor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630840,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For a large range of initial conditions, the system evolves into a state on this attractor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636240,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now remember: all the paths traced out here never cross and they never connect to form a loop,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641320,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If they did then they would continue on that loop forever and the behavior would be periodic and predictable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so each path here is actually an infinite curve in a finite space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652560,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how is that possible?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654240,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fractals. But that's a story for another video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656880,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this particular attractor is called the Lorenz attractor,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659680,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Probably the most famous example of a chaotic attractor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662560,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "though many others have been found for other systems of equations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666120,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now if people have heard anything about the butterfly effect,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668480,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's usually about how tiny causes make the future unpredictable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672560,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the science behind the butterfly effect also reveals a deep and beautiful structure underlying the dynamics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 679480,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One that can provide useful insights into the behavior of a system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683520,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can't predict how any individual state will evolve,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687040,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but you can say how a collection of states evolves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690360,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and, at least in the case of Lorenz's equations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693360,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they take the shape of a butterfly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699280,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey this part of the video is sponsored by LastPass,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702040,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the password manager with unlimited password storage and free cross-device sync"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706480,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before I used a password manager, I've got to admit, I used the same password for a lot of different accounts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712880,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I know that is incredibly dangerous because if even one of those sites got hacked,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716640,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then all of my important accounts would be exposed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719800,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quite the butterfly effect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721960,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "LastPass auto generates strong passwords for you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725440,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you have a different, indecipherable code for each website"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 729000,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and let's face it: if there's anything in your life that you want to be chaotic,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732360,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is the characters in your passwords"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735040,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the best part is because it autofills user names and passwords on websites"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739240,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or on iOS or Android apps and mobile sites,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 742280,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you never have to remember another password again. Not for the rest of your life"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747160,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that means no more writing down passwords, no more getting locked out of accounts,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751640,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no more password resets. You can use your brain for what it's meant to be doing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if you want extra features like advanced multi-factor authentication,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759400,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can upgrade to LastPass premium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761640,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I got to say, it works like magic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763280,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so put your passwords on autopilot with LastPass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766120,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Click the link below to find out more,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767840,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and thanks to LastPass for sponsoring this part of the video"
    } ]
  } ]
}
